depgraph: reuse whole backtracking attempts across a prune_rebuilds restart

Sub-series: P (stage 5) - patch 1 of 3; applies without 0036 and 0037, in any order with them.
Base: upstream bdf046b03 with 0001-0034.

After a prune_rebuilds restart the Backtracker hands out parameter sets that
differ from an earlier attempt in nothing except prune_rebuilds=True. The flag
is read at one place, at the end of _resolve() (now _resolve_after_prune_check),
after the graph is built and the merge list is serialized. _AttemptMemo keeps
the last 8 depgraphs built with prune_rebuilds=False and, for equal parameters
(contents and iteration order), hands the old depgraph out again or, when that
attempt ended in the prune restart, undoes the three statements of that branch
and runs the rest of _resolve(). Not active under --debug or without
backtracking.

Lock-step check: _verify_attempt_memo (PORTAGE_STAGE5_VERIFY=1 or "memo" in the
environment) builds every reused attempt from nothing as well and compares the
two depgraphs object by object (_emerge/_attempt_memo_verify.py); it raises
AssertionError on a difference. New test: tests/resolver/test_attempt_memo.py.

Six-state sum, stage 5 judge: 93.0 -> 76.3 s. Alone beside the unchanged series
on 2026-11-24: 88.8 -> 79.7 s and 90.6 -> 87.3 s (second pass on a loaded host).
Lock-step run on the six states: no difference.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, stage 5, 2026-11-24
(two rounds of implementer agents, black-box tester agents and a timing judge);
split into independent patches and re-checked on 2026-11-24. Not a human-written
change. Base: upstream bdf046b03 with patches 0001-0034. Test: `emerge -p -uND
@world` on six states of one system image, six resolves in parallel; every run
gave the same merge list in order and the same number of backtracking attempts
as unpatched bdf046b03.

--- a/lib/_emerge/_attempt_memo_verify.py
